        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.24000000000001,
          "end": 119.52000000000001,
          "en": "With that, we got this main header here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 121.743,
          "en": "but this button of course doesn't work yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.49,
          "en": "To make it work, this button now also needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.49,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "to set this state that shows or hides the modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "The modal is visible state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 134.67,
          "en": "however that state is in the PostsList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.67,
          "end": 137.1,
          "en": "But you learned how this problem can be fixed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.1,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "You can lift the state up, we can cut this state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 145.86,
          "en": "from PostsList and move it into the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.86,
          "end": 149.14,
          "en": "And there we then also must import useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 154.653,
          "en": "from react to make that useState hook available there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 162.44,
          "en": "We then also must cut the HideModalHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 168.14,
          "en": "and move that to app and also already add a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.72,
          "end": 172.07999999999998,
          "en": "called showModalHandler, which does the opposite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.07999999999998,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "of HideModalHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 176.823,
          "en": "It simply sets modalIsVisible to true again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "And now we just need to make sure that the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "whether the modal should be visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 186.183,
          "en": "or not is available in the PostsList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 190.47,
          "en": "Now to make it available there, we can use props again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.47,
          "end": 194.82,
          "en": "we can add a new prop, isPosting could be the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 198.16,
          "en": "You could also stick to modalIsVisible alternatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 201.75,
          "en": "but here I'll use isPosting as a prop name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.75,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "and that should be true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "and I'll use it down there in my conditional rendering code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 210.3,
          "en": "So if this is true, the modal should be displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.3,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "because if I am posting, I'm working on a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "So then this form should be displayed and if it's false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 217.623,
          "en": "it should not be displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.55,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "And in the app component we can now set this new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 224.04,
          "en": "isPosting prop on PostsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.04,
          "end": 227.94,
          "en": "And simply forward our modalIsVisible value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.94,
          "end": 232.65,
          "en": "So set the value of this state as a value for this prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.65,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "And with that we're passing the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 238.413,
          "en": "whether the modal should be visible or not to PostsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.85,
          "end": 241.65,
          "en": "Of course now we also must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "that we can talk into the opposite direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 246.06,
          "en": "So if the modal is closed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.06,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "we wanna trigger hideModalHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 250.8,
          "en": "If the backdrop is clicked, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.8,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "and in the main header, if the button is clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 256.683,
          "en": "I wanna show the modal again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.88,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "Now here in MainHeader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 263.31,
          "en": "I already do expect to get a onCreatePost prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.31,
          "end": 266.4,
          "en": "which I forward to onClick on that button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 268.08,
          "en": "So here I want to have a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.08,
          "end": 271.443,
          "en": "at that function that should make the modal visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.28,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "So therefore back in App.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "we can add the onCreatePost prop to MainHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "We can set that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 283.383,
          "en": "and set it to showModalHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.62,
          "end": 287.04,
          "en": "So that this function so that this function is passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.04,
          "end": 289.8,
          "en": "as a value to onCreatePost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.8,
          "end": 292.8,
          "en": "And on the PostsList component, we could add another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.8,
          "end": 297.8,
          "en": "prop called onStopPosting and here pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.8,
          "end": 301.833,
          "en": "the hideModalHandler function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.06,
          "end": 305.399,
          "en": "Now we just have to make sure that we use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.399,
          "end": 310.399,
          "en": "onStopPosting function in PostsList and therefore there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.65,
          "end": 313.413,
          "en": "again we can accept it as a new prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.03,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "And then here for modal for the onClose prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 324.98,
          "en": "we now pass the onStopPosting value to the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 327.03,
          "end": 331.02,
          "en": "so that in the end the onClose prop of the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.02,
          "end": 334.023,
          "en": "receives this hideModalHandler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 335.28,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "And passing these different functions across multiple levels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "of components and passing these different state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.54,
          "end": 346.32,
          "en": "around of course can be confusing at first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 346.32,
          "end": 348.72,
          "en": "So therefore it's just important to keep in mind that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 348.72,
          "end": 352.23,
          "en": "in the end we're just passing values around so that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 352.23,
          "end": 354.9,
          "en": "in the different components we can use exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 354.9,
          "end": 357.33299999999997,
          "en": "the values that should be used there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 358.2,
          "end": 359.13,
          "en": "By the way, the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.13,
          "end": 362.82,
          "en": "that my custom props here that take functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 362.82,
          "end": 365.88,
          "en": "as values like onCreatePost are called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 365.88,
          "end": 370.38,
          "en": "onCreatePost is just a convention I'm following.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 370.38,
          "end": 373.35,
          "en": "I could also just name it createPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 373.35,
          "end": 377.26,
          "en": "and update the name here in MainHeader of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 378.33,
          "end": 380.13,
          "en": "and that would work as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 380.13,
          "end": 382.23,
          "en": "However, it's a common convention to start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 382.23,
          "end": 384.75,
          "en": "with on in your prop name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 384.75,
          "end": 389.19,
          "en": "If that prop is receiving a function as a value to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 389.19,
          "end": 392.04,
          "en": "in the end make it clear that this prop won't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 392.04,
          "end": 395.13,
          "en": "with any other value, and in the end will typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 395.13,
          "end": 397.29,
          "en": "link that function that is received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 400.92,
          "en": "as a value to some event listener further down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 400.92,
          "end": 402.993,
          "en": "in your JSX component code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.43,
          "end": 406.71,
          "en": "However, now with all these changes made",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 406.71,
          "end": 408.69,
          "en": "if you save all your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.69,
          "end": 412.40999999999997,
          "en": "we can close that modal and we can also open it again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 412.40999999999997,
          "end": 417.40999999999997,
          "en": "So that's now working and therefore now back in App.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 418.02,
          "end": 419.82,
          "en": "we can also also switch the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 419.82,
          "end": 423.78,
          "en": "for modal is visible from true to false to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 423.78,
          "end": 428.22,
          "en": "that initially if we reload this page, no modal is visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 428.22,
          "end": 431.16,
          "en": "but if you click that post we see it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 431.16,
          "end": 433.95,
          "en": "and then there we can still add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 433.95,
          "end": 438.95,
          "en": "and add our text as we need to and update this first post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 439.77,
          "end": 443.22,
          "en": "And therefore that's yet another huge step forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 443.22,
          "end": 447.21,
          "en": "with more state passing across different components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
